Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:53:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(import): judge a closed shell's seams face by face;
 refuse only a real gap

The first closed-shell law counted every edge not used exactly twice in
opposite directions as open, and refused two healthy CAD exports. Each
pass now keeps the facet range of every face, and the seams between faces
are told apart:

- a face wound against its neighbours (a shared edge running the same
  way twice) is flipped to agree with them, and each connected group is
  turned to enclose a positive volume; logged, not refused;
- a boundary split differently on each side (T-junctions) is closed when
  every boundary edge's ends and midpoint lie within two chord tolerances
  of another face's boundary;
- only a boundary edge farther than that from every other face is a gap,
  refused with the face that owns most of them and the widest distance.

Open shells keep the kernel's winding and only refuse a dropped face.

Refs #1573

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
