From e2e60f51464662a75f811be8139685e68d461361 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:37:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(import): flip STEP faces deterministically; outward
 once per shell; say flips by name

Second review of PR #1576 (pullrequestreview-5900373722):
- The orientation solve is deterministic: votes in an ordered map, boundary
  segments and shells sorted, and the flips decided by a parity union-find
  that joins face pairs strongest evidence first (exact shared edges, then
  T-junction votes, then face numbers). 10208.STEP gave two flip sets over
  three runs before.
- Each connected group keeps the kernel's winding on its majority side;
  outward is decided once, from the whole shell's signed volume, and only
  when some face is flipped. A cavity wound inward and a lone curved face
  keep their winding.
- A shared edge still running the same way in both faces after the flips
  is refused by name; a T-junction-only disagreement is said in the notes.
- Flips are said by name in the import result: Graded::notes,
  ImportModel::notes, the MCP/script import_model answer and the status
  line. The gap width is measured over every gap edge (bounded work).

Refs #1573

